# Build trees owned by this repository.
build/
rust/target/
BUILD_OK
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The engine is the upstream box64 submodule at vendor/box64 (pinned by the
# gitlink to v0.4.2, see .gitmodules). `make
# patch` applies patches/ into that worktree, `make graft` links this
# repository's sources into it, and `make` builds under
# vendor/box64/build{,-pic}. None of that is superproject content: .gitmodules
# marks the submodule `ignore = untracked`, so its build trees, graft symlinks
# and generated heads never appear here; the submodule pointer is the only
# tracked fact.

# Tree-out patch scratch (appended, not a rewrite of the rules above). patches/
# work/ holds per-patch working drafts — e.g. patches/work/0020/signals.c.0020,
# a pre/post revision of the vendored file an in-flight patch is cut against.
# Those are generated scratch, not queue entries: only patches/NNNN-*.patch is a
# queue artifact. Ignoring the directory keeps the
# drafts out of git without deleting them; the pattern is anchored to
# /patches/work/ so it ignores nothing else under patches/.
/patches/work/
